It looks like the codepath taken is this:
https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/blob/6f50fb8ff53fb1a29f3c94479f1a199a1bc38452/py-polars/src/apply/lazy.rs#L45

Which ends up calling:
https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/blob/6f50fb8ff53fb1a29f3c94479f1a199a1bc38452/py-polars/src/conversion.rs#L687

Adding in some `dbg!()` calls  in `get_struct()` show the correct order, however `pyseries.series` has the field names sorted.

Which suggests this may happen in the `PySeries` creation part?

**Update:** It appears to be happening in this function:

https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/blob/6f50fb8ff53fb1a29f3c94479f1a199a1bc38452/py-polars/src/apply/mod.rs#L55

From a quick search, it seems a BTreeMap does not maintain insertion order and this appears to be where the "sorting" happens?

```rust
